# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
ignore:
  # Dev-only, and there is no in-range fix. @vitest/mocker ships as part of
  # vitest, which this repo pins to the exact version 2.1.9 in five manifests
  # (root, ag-charts-community, ag-charts-core, ag-charts-enterprise,
  # ag-charts-website). The advisory is fixed in 4.1.11, two majors up, so there
  # is no range to relock within - clearing it means a deliberate vitest 4.x
  # upgrade with config and snapshot-format changes across every suite, which is
  # scheduled work rather than a dependency bump.
  #
  # vitest is a test-runner devDependency and reaches no published bundle: every
  # published package depends only on other ag-charts-* packages plus tslib,
  # except ag-charts-server-side (jsdom, skia-canvas). Confirmed outside the
  # published production closure - a BFS from tslib, jsdom and skia-canvas covers
  # 72 packages and contains no vitest.
  #
  # Path is `*` deliberately: a versioned path silently stops matching the moment
  # a parent version moves, which is how four ignores in this repo had already
  # died unnoticed.
  SNYK-JS-VITESTMOCKER-19497933:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
            Dev-only test-runner dependency, absent from AG Charts runtime bundles and from
            the published production dependency closure. No in-range fix exists: vitest is
            pinned to exactly 2.1.9 and the advisory is fixed in 4.1.11, so remediation is a
            two-major vitest upgrade scheduled as its own work, not a bump. Time-boxed.
        expires: '2027-03-02T00:00:00.000Z'
        created: '2026-09-02T00:00:00.000Z'
  # FALSE POSITIVE - a working entry must live in THIS file, not the repo root.
  # `snyk test --yarn-workspaces` reads each workspace project's own .snyk, so a
  # root-level ignore never reaches this project. The path is `*` on purpose: the
  # advisory's vulnerable range is `*`, the finding is the package NAME itself, and
  # a versioned path goes stale on every beta bump - which is exactly how the
  # previous `ag-charts-test@14.0.0-beta.20260712` entry silently stopped matching.
  #
  # `ag-charts-test` is our own private, never-published workspace package
  # (libraries/ag-charts-test, "private": true). Snyk matches it by name against a
  # malicious `ag-charts-test` published to npm to impersonate AG Charts: version
  # 99.9.1 on 2026-07-07 (an absurdly high version, the dependency-confusion
  # signature), which npm removed on 2026-07-10, leaving a 0.0.1-security
  # placeholder that also blocks re-registration. We never fetch it - the name
  # resolves to the local workspace and our pin is exact - so there is nothing to
  # upgrade and no fix version exists.
  SNYK-JS-AGCHARTSTEST-17950302:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
            False positive - name collision with a malicious npm package. This is our own
            private workspace package (libraries/ag-charts-test, private: true), never
            published and never fetched from npm, and it is dev/test-only tooling absent
            from AG Charts runtime bundles. No fix version exists - nothing to upgrade.
        expires: '2027-03-02T00:00:00.000Z'
        created: '2026-09-02T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-POSTCSS-18313038:
    - vitest@2.1.9 > vite@6.3.5 > postcss@8.5.3:
        reason: >-
            Used in build & dev - not included in final production build
        expires: 2027-03-02T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-07-27T10:17:20.151Z
  SNYK-JS-POSTCSS-18313036:
    - vitest@2.1.9 > vite@6.3.5 > postcss@8.5.3:
        reason: >-
            Used in build & dev - not included in final production build
        expires: 2027-03-02T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-07-27T10:16:26.706Z
